      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the shelf life of Ghar Aangan Ghee?",
            "answer": "<p>Pure, hand-churned ghee is highly stable and does not spoil easily. It can last up to 12-18 months at room temperature. Keep it in a dry, dark place and always use a clean, dry spoon to extend its shelf life.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is Badri cow ghee considered premium?",
            "answer": "<p>Badri cows are native Himalayan humped cattle that graze on pristine Himalayan pastures, herbs, and local flora. They yield a very small daily quantity of milk, which is exceptionally rich in nutrients and A2 beta-casein proteins.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it need refrigeration?",
            "answer": "<p>No, pure ghee does not require refrigeration. In fact, storing it in the fridge will alter its granular texture. It is best stored in its original glass jar in your kitchen pantry.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is Pahadi Gud (Traditional Jaggery) prepared?",
            "answer": "<p>Our traditional jaggery is made by slow wood-fired boiling of fresh sugarcane juice, unrefined and chemical-free. We blend it with native mountain herbs, seeds, and premium dry fruits (like Kaju, Badam, Kismis, and Saunf) to create delicious, mineral-rich sweetener options.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Pisyu Loon (Salts) and Mandua Flour?",
            "answer": "<p>Pisyu Loon is Uttarakhand's heritage salt, hand-crushed on traditional stone (Sil-Batta) with native mountain herbs, seeds (like Bhaang/Hemp), and chilis. Mandua Ka Aata (Ragi) is high-altitude, stone-ground finger millet flour that is naturally gluten-free and rich in calcium, iron, and fiber.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are the pulses and fruit juices organic and natural?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! Our Heritage Dals & Pulses (like Rajma, Bhatt Ki Dal, Gauhat, and Lobia) are mountain-grown, unpolished, and protein-dense. Our Fruit Juices & Squashes (like Buransh/Rhododendron, Amla, and Orange) are crafted from wild-harvested Himalayan fruits and flowers, rich in Vitamin C and antioxidants.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
